<title>MEXICO: Latin American raw steel output by nation - ILAFA.</title>
<headline>Latin American raw steel output by nation - ILAFA.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latin American Insitute of Iron and Steel (ILAFA) outlined here at the Latin American Steel Congress production by country in the region. A table follows with a breakdown in 1000s of tonnes. The figure for 1996 is preliminary.</p>
<p>  Country	 1994     1995     1996   %Chnge 96/95</p>
<p>  Argentina     3,314    3,852    4,000	3.8</p>
<p>  Brazil	 25,747   25,076   25,300	0.9</p>
<p>  Chile	   1,041    1,018    1,135     11.5</p>
<p>  Colombia	  691	792	831	5.0</p>
<p>  Mexico	 10,260   12,090   12,600	4.2</p>
<p>  Peru		506	510	530	3.9</p>
<p>  Venezuela     3,521    3,634    4,070     12.0</p>
<p>  Others	    934    1,119    1,175	5.0</p>
<p>  Total	  46,014   48,091   49,641	3.2</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530</p>
</text>
